@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: re-architect how proveo's kit v3 workloads get every subscription and API key, as sbx-native as sbx allows
' PLANNED — nothing here is implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
'   the shipped state this replaces ... _spec/internal/sbx/credential-resolution.puml (L1–L6, R1–R8, O1–O4)
'   local edits to upstream kits ...... _spec/internal/sbx/vendored-kit-deltas.puml
'   the earlier custody plans ......... _spec/_plans/secret-custody.puml, _spec/_plans/host-held-provider-keys.puml,
'                                       _spec/_plans/init-credential-provisioning.puml
'
' ── THE REQUEST ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The Executor, 2026-10-28: "plan to re-architect how credentials are stored in
' our sbx kit v3 for all subscriptions & keys". Standing constraints: "support
' only kit v3"; "Keep credentials as `sbx` native as possible".
'
' ── UPSTREAM, READ 2026-10-28 ──────────────────────────────────────────────
' docker/sandbox-kit-spec docs/spec/capabilities/com.docker.sandbox/credential@1.md:
'   `service` "Lowercase-kebab name in the host credential store" — any id, not
'     only sbx's built-in list. "A Kit declares the need, the user's bindings
'     answer it." "Host environment variables never auto-inject."
'   "MUST fail resolution when a required entry has no binding; an optional
'     entry with no binding is skipped and recorded, and the Kit runs
'     unauthenticated."
'   "Two Kits declaring the same (service, phase) is a composition conflict".
' docker/sbx-kits-contrib spec/bindings/types.go (~/.config/sbx/credentials.yaml):
'   "A block's presence is the approval: ApiKey present ⟺ inject the stored
'     secret … OAuth present ⟺ the user approved OAuth for this service".
'   `remembered` (workspace → binding variant) is "Not consulted by resolution yet".
' docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/security/credentials/:
'   "Prefer the service-based flow whenever it's an option"; custom secrets are
'     "experimental … may change without notice".
'   "Third-party kits require an approved binding for each credential they use";
'     non-interactive: "the sandbox starts with the credential withheld".
'   "Sandbox-scoped secrets take precedence over global secrets." Service-secret
'     changes "take effect in existing local sandboxes without a restart."
'   Dynamic sources: `--ref` (op://, AWS ARN) and `--command`; "Resolution and
'     caching happen on the host"; cached 55m, `--refresh on-demand` per use.
'   OAuth: Codex ahead of time `sbx secret set openai --oauth`; Claude Code
'     `/login` in the sandbox; Cursor and Droid "have no ahead-of-time option".
'   "When both resolve at runtime, the API key takes precedence and OAuth acts
'     as the fallback."
' MEASURED here: proveo never reads or writes credentials.yaml (no Go caller).
'   This Mac's file binds openai to apiKey ONLY, so an opencode run here would
'   withhold the ChatGPT OAuth that Fedora's binding allowed. [Inference] the
'   Fedora file carries an openai oauth block; not read.
'
' ── TARGET: PROVEO DECLARES, THE USER STORES AND BINDS, sbx RESOLVES ────────
'   L3 store     one entry per SERVICE id (registry id = service id), written
'                by sbx's own commands: `sbx secret set <svc>` (stdin, --ref,
'                --command), `sbx secret set openai --oauth`, an in-sandbox
'                sign-in sbx captures. proveo writes no value on a run.
'   bindings     credentials.yaml decides apiKey vs OAuth per service. The
'                subscription/key choice lives HERE, not in which entries exist.
'   L4 declare   every provider proveo supports is a credential@1 entry with
'                `optional: true`: upstream's for its services, proveo's for the
'                rest (moonshot, opencode, zai, …) — no set-custom.
'   L5/L6        sbx renders; the agent's own login cannot outrank sbx's in a
'                managed mode (codex's guard, extended); proveo READS both after
'                start and reports the credential in use.
'
' ── CHANGES, EACH WITH WHAT IT DELETES ─────────────────────────────────────
' C1 ONE ROUTE FOR EVERY KEY. Declare credential@1 per registry provider with a
'    service id, inject rules from internal/provider, `optional: true`. Store
'    with `sbx secret set <id>`. sbx validates no name (MEASURED, R7).
'    Deletes: customSecretTarget, sbx.SecretSetCustom(Args), CustomSecretPlaceholder,
'    BuiltinServices as a routing switch. Gate: M1.
' C2 SERVICE NAMES ONLY. `proveo init` writes the service id and nothing else.
'    Deletes: credSlot.Also, the subscription store names in StoreName
'    (subscriptionName), and offers `sbx secret rm` for existing aliases.
'    Gate: M2.
' C3 NO VALUES THROUGH PROVEO WHERE sbx CAN SOURCE THEM (F3). `proveo init` registers
'    a source, not a copy: `--ref op://…`, `--command '<resolver>'` (keychain:,
'    pass: become commands); a plain env value goes through stdin once.
'    Runs stop writing the store: Spec's per-run secrets loop goes.
'    Deletes: the secrets loop in sandbox.go, internal/secretref's run-time
'    resolution for provider keys (kept only if a non-provider use remains).
'    Gate: M3.
' C4 SUBSCRIPTIONS ARE sbx OAuth, NOTHING ELSE. Per harness, proveo prints the
'    sbx-native sign-in (codex/opencode-openai: `sbx secret set openai --oauth`;
'    claudecode: `/login` in the sandbox; cursor: its own prompt) and never
'    reads a host OAuth blob.
'    Deletes: ReadKeychainLogin and the Keychain blob path, CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
'    as a stored credential (it maps to no service; O2). Gate: M4.
' C5 THE CHOICE IS A BINDING. "Use my subscription" = the service's binding has
'    an oauth block and no apiKey block; "use my key" = the reverse. proveo
'    reads credentials.yaml, shows per service which mechanism is approved and
'    which is stored, and refuses a run whose required mechanism is unbound,
'    instead of letting sbx withhold it silently. proveo never writes bindings (F1).
' C6 RUN-LOCAL OVERRIDES ARE SANDBOX-SCOPED (F2). A per-run key (`--credentials`
'    with a value only this run should use) goes in with `--sandbox <name>`,
'    which outranks the global entry and leaves with the sandbox. Ends R7's
'    "one run's write authenticates every later sandbox". Gate: M5.
' C7 THE AGENT CANNOT OUTRANK sbx. opencode and cursor kits get codex's guard
'    (block an agent-owned login while SBX_CRED_<SVC>_MODE is apikey|oauth), as
'    an upstream PR carried as a vendored delta. Closes O3.
' C8 REPORT THE OUTCOME. After start, read SBX_CRED_*_MODE and the agent's own
'    export through `sbx exec` (read-only) and print the credential in use; warn
'    on a mismatch with the bound mechanism.
'
' ── P0 DONE 2026-10-28 — results in credential-resolution.puml (P0 MEASUREMENTS) ─
'   M1 ✓ any service id injects once bound → C1 cleared.
'   M2 ✓ env-var-named entries are never read → C2 cleared (delete the aliases).
'   M3 ✓ on macOS (`security … -w`, on-demand refresh reaches a running sandbox);
'        Linux `pass` still open → C3 cleared for darwin.
'   M4 ✓ the global OAuth slot reaches a fresh sandbox → C4 cleared; the
'        in-sandbox `/login` was not driven (needs a person).
'   M5 ✓ --sandbox works before create, overrides live, falls back on rm, and
'        dies with the sandbox → C6 cleared.
'   New: O5 (SBX_CRED_ANTHROPIC_MODE=none while OAuth injects) and O6 (an
'   unbound key still exports its sentinel) feed C5's refusal: proveo must read
'   the binding, because neither the store nor the env var tells the truth.
'
' ── P1 DONE 2026-10-28 — credential-resolution.puml R9, R10 ─────────────────
'   C5 read side: refuseUnboundCredential (was reportCredentials) + unboundRefusal; `sbx create` gets the
'      terminal so sbx's consent prompt shows (F1).
'   C8: reportCredentialInUse after the session (opencode, codex, claudecode).
'   Correction from P1's live run: approvals gate the API key only; the openai
'   OAuth login is used without an `oauth` block (M7). So "use my subscription"
'   is NOT a binding choice on sbx 0.50 — an approved key would win, so the
'   choice is whether the service holds an approved key. C5's wording below
'   predates M7.
'   Left for P2: run.go's "using <ENV_VAR> from sbx's stored credentials" line
'   reports an env-var-named entry, which M2 proved is never read; it now sits
'   above R9's truthful line and contradicts it.
'
' ── P2 DONE 2026-10-28 — credential-resolution.puml R2, R4 ─────────────────
'   C1: one route. customSecretTarget, sbx.SecretSetCustom(Args),
'      CustomSecretPlaceholder, SecretRemoveCustomArgs, BuiltinServices and
'      IsBuiltinService are deleted; agentCredentials declares a service the
'      store holds or this run stores, so a first run of a new provider works
'      once sbx's consent prompt approves it (R9).
'   C2: service ids only. provisionSlot writes s.Store alone (credSlot.Also
'      gone); StoreName lost its def argument and subscriptionName; StoreHolds
'      and NoCredentialHint work in services; sbx.StoredSecretNames is deleted
'      for sbx.StoredServices. `proveo init` lists stale entries with their
'      `sbx secret rm` and removes none.
'   Pulled forward from C4: a plan token is never stored, and init's
'      subscription row for claudecode, codex and cursor is a locked sign-in row.
'   run.go's stale "using <ENV_VAR> from sbx's stored credentials" line now
'      names the service and defers to R9's lines.
'
' ── P3 DONE 2026-10-28 — credential-resolution.puml R7, R8, R11, R12 ───────
'   C3/F3: secretref.SbxSource maps keychain:/pass:/cmd:/op:///AWS ARN to sbx
'      --command/--ref; ProviderLookup returns references unresolved; the
'      Resolver, Outcome and Advice are deleted. `proveo init` registers a
'      reference as a global sbx source.
'   C6/F2: a run's secrets go `--sandbox <name>` (M5, M8); no run writes the
'      global store. The "host-wide and outlives this run" note is gone.
'   C4: ReadKeychainLogin, KeychainLogin, keychain.go and
'      PROVEO_KEYCHAIN_SERVICE are deleted; NeedsSandboxLogin (login.go) no
'      longer counts a plan token in the env; the hint prints sbx.SignIn.
'   Verification: TestAReferenceReachesTheSandboxAsAScopedSbxSource (e2e) PASSED
'      on macOS with a temporary probe binding; it skips with instructions when
'      the binding is absent. e2e/keychain_test.go (the resolver's) is deleted.
'   Still open: Linux `pass` (M3), O3 (P4), O5, O6.
'
' ── P4 DONE 2026-10-28 — vendored-kit-deltas.puml DELTA 2 ──────────────────
'   C7: opencode's import hook activates sbx-openai over an agent-owned login
'      (kept, inactive). Measured red on the upstream rule and green with the
'      delta in proveo/opencode:local; persisted as two TestImageOpencode checks.
'   cursor: no delta — its OAuth token endpoint is intercepted by sbx, and the
'      manifest scrubs .cursor/auth.json [Inference for the interception].
'   Upstream: the draft now carries DELTA 1 and DELTA 2; nothing filed.
'
' ── MEASUREMENTS BEFORE ANY CODE ───────────────────────────────────────────
' M1 a non-built-in id (`moonshot`): `sbx secret set moonshot` + a proveo
'    credential@1 service moonshot with inject rules → header injected? (N14
'    proved it for `opencode` only.)
' M2 a store holding ONLY `OPENAI_API_KEY` (no `openai` key): does any binding
'    read it? Expect SBX_CRED_OPENAI_MODE=none. Needs the operator's OK, since
'    the probe removes their `openai` entry temporarily.
' M3 `sbx secret set <svc> --command 'security find-generic-password -w …'`
'    on darwin and `pass show …` on Linux: verified at register, refreshed at
'    use, value never in proveo's process.
' M4 claudecode with only the in-sandbox `/login` (no CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN):
'    the credential survives a new sandbox (global OAuth slot).
' M5 `sbx secret set <svc> --sandbox <name>` before the sandbox's first start
'    vs after create: which works, and does removal restore the global entry.
'
' ── FORKS, DECIDED 2026-10-28 ──────────────────────────────────────────────
' F1 bindings writer → "sbx prompts, proveo reports". proveo never writes
'    credentials.yaml. It reads it, shows each service's approved mechanism,
'    and refuses a run whose required mechanism is unbound, printing how to
'    approve it. sbx's consent prompt stays the only writer.
'    (rejected: `proveo init` writes after a yes; proveo writes per run)
' F2 per-run values → "Sandbox-scoped only". A run normally writes nothing;
'    `proveo init` registers sources. A run-only key goes in with
'    `--sandbox <name>` (C6, gated on M5).
'    (rejected: never; keep the global write)
' F3 secretref → "Retire for provider keys". `proveo init` translates an
'    existing keychain:/cmd:/pass:/op:// reference into the matching sbx
'    source (`--ref` or `--command`) once; the provider-key path of
'    internal/secretref is then deleted.
'    (rejected: keep as the --command generator; keep as is)
'
' ── PHASES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' P0 M1–M5 — DONE 2026-10-28 (above).
' P1 C8 (read-only) and C5's read side: visibility first, nothing removed.
' P2 C1 + C2: one route, one name; migrate existing entries with printed
'    `sbx secret` commands.
' P3 C3 + C4 + C6: proveo stops carrying values and OAuth blobs.
' P4 C7 upstream PR + delta; drop the delta when upstream merges.
title sbx-native credential storage — proveo declares, the user binds, sbx resolves

actor "operator" as OP
component "proveo init\nregisters sources" as INIT <<app>>
database "sbx store\nservice ids only\n(value · --ref · --command · OAuth)" as STORE <<db>>
file "credentials.yaml\nbindings: apiKey | oauth per service" as BIND <<db>>
component "proveo workload\ncredential@1 per provider\noptional: true" as WL <<app>>
component "sbx proxy\nresolves on the host" as PROXY <<host>>
component "agent\nsentinels only" as AG <<cloud>>
component "proveo report\nSBX_CRED_*_MODE + agent export" as REP <<app>>

OP ARROW_MAIN INIT : sign-ins, keys
INIT ARROW_MAIN STORE : sbx secret set <svc> (--ref | --command | stdin | --oauth)
OP ARROW_MAIN BIND : approve mechanism (F1)
WL ARROW_MAIN PROXY : declares need
STORE ARROW_MAIN PROXY : by service
BIND ARROW_MAIN PROXY : gates mechanism
PROXY ARROW_MAIN AG : sentinel in, real value at egress
REP ARROW_OPTIONAL AG : read-only, after start

note right of BIND
  **The choice lives in the binding.**
  An API key outranks OAuth, so the
  subscription/key choice is which
  mechanism the user approved.
end note

note right of WL
  **One route for every provider.**
  credential@1 takes any service id;
  set-custom is experimental and
  goes (C1, gated on M1).
end note
@enduml
